{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it","id":1532650,"title":"Why the Apocalypse in the title matters and how W5 fails to address it","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-15T08:40:19-07:00","id":1532650,"title":"Why the Apocalypse in the title matters and how W5 fails to address it","content":"Even if it is by this point a joke, all WoD games have a title what creature it lets you play and then one of the core elements of it.<br /> <br /> Yet, it is odd that a werewolf game puts the end of the world as one of its most central concepts. After all, werewolves aren't really associated with the apocalypse in myths. The closest is Fenris-Ulf in Norse myths, but Fenris was a monstrous wolf, not a werewolf. Shouldn't Changing or Fury be a better descriptor?<br /> <br /> Well, WtA's werewolves draw from older material than the movies and the focus is not on being a werewolf. The focus is on the state of the world, the way nature is being destroyed and such. In the game, being a werewolf is more akin to a spiritual guardian than a cursed being.<br /> <br /> The Apocalypse in the title not only refers to the literal end of existence but to the little apocalypses happening every year. Species dying, people losing touch with their ancestral cultures, etc. WtA is about looking at the state of the world and feeling the horror of just how hard it is to fix it if not impossible. Never mind the sadly now very real horror of greed over care and ennui towards your fellow humans and nature.<br /> <br /> This genuine approach and call to action has, of course, created an opposite reaction that calls WtA's tone childish. More recently, as we actually start seeing the effects of climate change, the reactions have also become ones of denial, apathy and fear of doing the wrong thing.<br /> <br /> It is the latter that W5 shows the clearest in its depiction of the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> The apocalypse in W5 is invisible to normal people and other supernaturals. At most, it is the fall of the garou nation as the climate change happening in the real world. Despite this, W5 is very clear about discouraging its PCs from taking action further than locally.<br /> <br /> In effect, W5's apocalypse and what it wants the players to do about it is toothless. The game spends page space detailing what not to do, but very little on what to do and what the apocalypse looks like. Because it is afraid to take a stand, instead focusing on passive-aggressive remarks here and there.<br /> <br /> W5, despite its blurb stating it is about striking back at pollution, isn't willing to have its PCs be eco-terrorists (though some do slip through) and actively calls direct action the wrong method.<br /> <br /> It isn't just what W5 tells the PCs shouldn't do, it is also how much the PCs don't have to do. It's the end of the world as we know it and you can still go to McDonald's in peace. The world is lost and you still have to go to work. If we weren't told the apocalypse was raging, we'd assume it was still in the future. The game is, intentionally or unintentionally, saying that there is no need to do anything. Even if the world is ending, it won't inconvenience you.<br /> <br /> To put things plainly, W5's apocalypse is the way it is so there won't be paid sick days for the employees. It is an end that preserves and protects the status quo.<br /> <br /> Of course, an apocalypse that changes nothing is not really an apocalypse. Indeed, W5 wears the apocalypse label more out of legacy than any real intention of addressing it. It wants to focus on werewolf packs and caern tending, not something as serious as the fate of the world.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'd say W5 doesn't want to be about the garou at all but instead about werewolves. It wants to be Werewolf the Fury.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T08:58:25-07:00","id":1532651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it#post1532650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact, I'd say W5 doesn't want to be about the garou at all but instead about werewolves. It wants to be Werewolf the Fury.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I love w5 a great deal,i consider justin achilli a friend. But i agree with this criticism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T09:00:31-07:00","id":1532652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it#post1532650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W5, despite its blurb stating it is about striking back at pollution, isn't willing to have its PCs be eco-terrorists (though some do slip through) and actively calls direct action the wrong method.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This one however is not really how I've read it. I think it's more accurate to say that w5 states Direct Action is something the Garou are not <i>good </i>at.<br /> The same way the Kindred are not great at being nice, the Garou usually fail when they try Direct Action, Direct Action just iisn't their area of expertise because while they are good at killing,they don't realize killing people and destroying machines won't solve anything. in fact you can make a good argument that killing people and destroying machines only makes things worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T09:45:22-07:00","id":1532653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532652#post1532652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This one however is not really how I've read it. I think it's more accurate to say that w5 states Direct Action is something the Garou are not <i>good </i>at.<br /> The same way the Kindred are not great at being nice, the Garou usually fail when they try Direct Action, Direct Action just iisn't their area of expertise because while they are good at killing,they don't realize killing people and destroying machines won't solve anything. in fact you can make a good argument that killing people and destroying machines only makes things worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's wrong, though, because destroying machines and other acts of sabotage can absolutely solve problems. When value is only placed in property and capital, destroying it is the most effective protest. Glass Walkers gain extra points only because they can make machines effectively inoperable with a wiggle of the nose. Ragabash, however, have historically been able to absolutely brick important materiel for good just by touching it (Gremlins).<br /> <br /> Seriously, how is it that literal Monkeywrenching became something that couldn't solve problems? It buys time, it hits the company in the only place that it feels anything like pain, and eventually could cause insurance companies to break off relationships with them. If the business apparatus is not willing to break off relations with a company on the basis of said company being scum, target the scum (and then move on to the rest of the apparatus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T09:52:48-07:00","id":1532654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532653#post1532653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's wrong, though, because destroying machines and other acts of sabotage can absolutely solve problems. When value is only placed in property and capital, destroying it is the most effective protest. Glass Walkers gain extra points only because they can make machines effectively inoperable with a wiggle of the nose. Ragabash, however, have historically been able to absolutely brick important materiel for good just by touching it (Gremlins).<br /> <br /> Seriously, how is it that literal Monkeywrenching became something that couldn't solve problems? It buys time, it hits the company in the only place that it feels anything like pain, and eventually could cause insurance companies to break off relationships with them. If the business apparatus is not willing to break off relations with a company on the basis of said company being scum, target the scum (and then move on to the rest of the apparatus).</div> </div> </div> </div>that's a good debate to have,unfortunately is not one i can have rn. sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T12:36:44-07:00","id":1532662,"title":"","content":"To be honest I feel that Fifth Edition might have made more sense of it were named - or renamed - WEREWOLF: THE GAUNTLET (Since this emphasises the grinding nature of Garou life in this take on the setting, as well as the much more pronounced divide between the Realms of the Spirit and the Material Realm).<br /> <br /> As for how THE APOCALYPSE became a core part of WEREWOLF, I do suspect a debt of inspiration from Norse Mythology - since the Age of Ragnarok is called \u201c\u2026 a wind age, a WOLF age\u2026\u201d in the Eddas and it\u2019s not just Fenris playing his part in the End Times (The wolves that eat the Sun &amp; Moon come to mind); assuming you want to make things a little less culturally-specific (At least in the English language) APOCALYPSE is probably the best option, which generates it\u2019s own cascade of possibilities.<br /> <br /> How things took a turn for the CAPTAIN PLANET is still an interesting question, though!\ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T12:47:28-07:00","id":1532663,"title":"","content":"The environmentalist angle isn't really that difficult of a question to answer:<br /> <br /> The initial premise of the WoD was to play as the monsters, but make them sympathetic in some way and the primary PCs be &quot;dark grey&quot; to the &quot;pitch black&quot; morality of their main antagonists. The games were unabashedly political and used political and activist causes as central themes to the playable supernaturals as the thing that made them sympathetic despite their monstrosity. While things changed over time, the WoD began as a 90s counter-culture release value where your PCs had the power to viscerally engage with systems that were failing society. Connecting werewolves to the wilderness and thus making them creatures that want to protect the environment from human encroachment is a simple leap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T22:38:46-07:00","id":1532683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532653#post1532653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's wrong, though, because destroying machines and other acts of sabotage can absolutely solve problems. When value is only placed in property and capital, destroying it is the most effective protest. Glass Walkers gain extra points only because they can make machines effectively inoperable with a wiggle of the nose. Ragabash, however, have historically been able to absolutely brick important materiel for good just by touching it (Gremlins).<br /> <br /> Seriously, how is it that literal Monkeywrenching became something that couldn't solve problems? It buys time, it hits the company in the only place that it feels anything like pain, and eventually could cause insurance companies to break off relationships with them. If the business apparatus is not willing to break off relations with a company on the basis of said company being scum, target the scum (and then move on to the rest of the apparatus).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, in real life, a lot of crisis actors drive protestors to action that is designed to vilify them. Because, yes, the real change is at the ballot box and contract signings.<br /> <br /> Corporate folk LOVE making the environmentalists into violent loonies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T01:00:55-07:00","id":1532685,"title":"","content":"I think W5 is more concerned with lambasting Garou as a concept than anything else. The game's pessimistic take has to be considered in the context of the game also pushing hard for Garou-PCs to do nothing but confirm these pessimistic notions. Rage and violence are still at the heart of the game. The tools the game gives to players push into that direction and <i>only </i>that direction. Deemphasizing the Umbra, taking away Gnosis, making Garou more reliant on Rage mechanically and no outline for solutions that wouldn't involve destruction only serve to highlight that.<br /> <br /> So, I think as far as the environmentalist angle is concerned, the game has more to say about the idea of rage-fueled shapeshifting monsters trying to do environmental activism than environmental activism itself. The game ignores that angle as the game is instead about what the rage-fueled monsters do and how that's bad. W5 is a game that asks the players &quot;When will you Rage?&quot; and then when the players answer that question is telling them they've done something wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T03:08:55-07:00","id":1532693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532683#post1532683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Corporate folk LOVE making the environmentalists into violent loonies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find myself thinking that the perspective that causing damage to a machine, specifically targeted with a purpose that renders it inoperable, constitutes an act of violence is an example of corporate propaganda actually winning.<br /> <br /> We can say that change takes place at the ballot box, but that would kind of come across as a long term solution even if it was working, which... it kind of isn't. A number of protestors marching into a mining site, walking past the workers in a mass that security guards can't really do anything about (obviating the need to do anything to actually stop them harmfully) and disabling the machinery would be pretty immediate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T09:23:26-07:00","id":1532702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532685#post1532685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I think as far as the environmentalist angle is concerned, the game has more to say about the idea of rage-fueled shapeshifting monsters trying to do environmental activism than environmental activism itself. The game ignores that angle as the game is instead about what the rage-fueled monsters do and how that's bad. W5 is a game that asks the players &quot;When will you Rage?&quot; and then when the players answer that question is telling them they've done something wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way the apocalypse is approached is still really interesting, because all of it is geared to be as little of an inconvenience as possible. It is like the game is detailing it out of a contract and would like to ignore it as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Which, given the times we live in, really says a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T10:44:03-07:00","id":1532704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532652#post1532652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one however is not really how I've read it. I think it's more accurate to say that w5 states Direct Action is something the Garou are not <i>good </i>at.<br /> The same way the Kindred are not great at being nice, the Garou usually fail when they try Direct Action, Direct Action just iisn't their area of expertise because while they are good at killing,they don't realize killing people and destroying machines won't solve anything. in fact you can make a good argument that killing people and destroying machines only makes things worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>If killing people and destroying machines didn't do anything militaries wouldn't do it. War is simply politics by other means, and peaceful ways of political change are foreclosed to the Gaians (I'm using the term here to refer to Gaian spirits, Fera, and Kinfolk). Legally, most of them aren't people and can be killed with impunity, those that are people often are politically marginalized, and their needs exist in direct contradiction to the demands of modern society... unless you're a Glass Walker, I guess. They can't admit they exist so they can't make any political demands, and given history we have no reason to believe that they'd be successful at making them either. They can't wait for conditions to change, either; they are being wiped out <i>right the fuck now</i>. And this is without even taking into account the Wyrm or Weaver! I don't think you can argue that violence isn't necessary for them, even though it isn't sufficient.<br /> <br /> And honestly? The Garou are fucking <i>awesome</i> at direct action. It gets more touch and go when other supernatural forces are involved, naturally, but if you gave anyone with a modicum of intelligence the services of five Garou with rudimentary self-control and a few brain cells to rub together they'd be utterly unstoppable. Surveillance? Have them take glabro form and the cops won't be looking for their homid form. Security checkpoints? Bypass them through the Umbra. Guards? Ask the local birds where they are and if they can help distract them. Clean-up? There's a talen capable of cleansing pollution from bodies of water. This is all stuff that can be done without tribe-specific gifts at character creation. Building new pipelines or mining projects would shortly grind to a halt.<br /> <br /> In comparison they kind of suck at normal politics. Rage means that they have to roll frenzy checks periodically and they're naturally off-putting to a certain percentage of people. Kinfolk don't have that problem but they're already sent to do normal politics. The Fera are the guys you want to handle the other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T11:12:26-07:00","id":1532707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532702#post1532702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way the apocalypse is approached is still really interesting, because all of it is geared to be as little of an inconvenience as possible. It is like the game is detailing it out of a contract and would like to ignore it as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Which, given the times we live in, really says a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think W5 has a good handle on the moral implications of its setting either because of that. &quot;The ends justify the means&quot; is normally considered a bad thing for good reasons. There are all sorts of problems with Utilitarianism and consequentialist moral equations in a normal scenario. After all, it's hard to look at any decision and have a complete knowledge of what the consequences are and so it's hard to weigh what exactly qualifies as the &quot;most good&quot; under the circumstances. That's the real world, though, and when you're describing a fictional setting that can become much more clear-cut. This is the case here. Before the Apocalypse was close but an avoidable and somewhat distant thing and so actions to prevent the Apocalypse could be questioned and judged accordingly as going too far. Meanwhile, W5, though, has raised the stakes and now it's the Age of Apocalypse and Garou know for a fact that the Apocalypse is nigh. Well, that actually makes the moral calculus far more complicated. Imagine any trolley-problem where one option is knowing for a fact that this path will lead to the end of everything in existence. A lot of things suddenly become justifiable in that context.<br /> <br /> And that, of course, brings up Hauglosk and W5's notion of Garou being the wrong tool for fixing the problems of the world. If this is truly the Age of Apocalypse and that is the end is truly nigh, I would say this would lead to a resurgence of relevance for Garou instead. In the end-times the Garou are a great tool to brutally and radically turn things around. Lots of norms can be tossed aside as the fate of all existence hangs in the balance. Same as the game doesn't fully grapple with what it means for the Garou-Nation to have fallen, it also doesn't deal with the full implications of an Age of Apocalypse as the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T12:37:24-07:00","id":1532717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532707#post1532707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same as the game doesn't fully grapple with what it means for the Garou-Nation to have fallen, it also doesn't deal with the full implications of an Age of Apocalypse as the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, in terms of a writing analysis, this is interesting. Because it is very clear they tried to do the V5 &quot;Gehenna came and went and now the problems are mundane&quot; thing and tried as hard as they could to remove any and all reasons for the PCs to take action beyond their own backyard.<br /> <br /> Like, the reason why the apocalypse is happening is not because they wanted to address it. It's like that because they wanted there to be absolutely no chance to affect things in the larger scale. The same reason the Nation was shattered, it was too global and too impactful.<br /> <br /> This is basically dooming the world, because doing something would matter too much. And boy what a message THAT is XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T12:50:12-07:00","id":1532718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532717#post1532717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, in terms of a writing analysis, this is interesting. Because it is very clear they tried to do the V5 &quot;Gehenna came and went and now the problems are mundane&quot; thing and tried as hard as they could to remove any and all reasons for the PCs to take action beyond their own backyard.<br /> <br /> Like, the reason why the apocalypse is happening is not because they wanted to address it. It's like that because they wanted there to be absolutely no chance to affect things in the larger scale. The same reason the Nation was shattered, it was too global and too impactful.<br /> <br /> This is basically dooming the world, because doing something would matter too much. And boy what a message THAT is XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Now it's starting to sound like they were aiming for a WoD version of Beast instead of another W:tA edition...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T12:53:45-07:00","id":1532719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532718#post1532718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now it's starting to sound like they were aiming for a WoD version of Beast instead of another W:tA edition...</div> </div> </div> </div>Something something no greater evil than someone just doing their job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T13:25:07-07:00","id":1532720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532717#post1532717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, in terms of a writing analysis, this is interesting. Because it is very clear they tried to do the V5 &quot;Gehenna came and went and now the problems are mundane&quot; thing and tried as hard as they could to remove any and all reasons for the PCs to take action beyond their own backyard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that but Gehenna-as-a-cycle is a bit in V5 that marks it as a continuation, something added to the canon of what came before. There's no reason to step things up similar to this in W5... Maybe this Age of Apocalypse is a game of telephone as concepts like that were first brought up by the By Nights Studio version of a new WtA-edition and by the time things got to the version the Paradox in-house team worked on, that idea just became a thoughtless auto-include, like everybody was acting like &quot;Yeah, of course, the new WtA-edition takes place during the Age of Apocalypse. It has always been thus.&quot;. And so nobody even questioned this part or why it is part of the new edition once we got to the people who worked on the version that was released.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532717#post1532717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, the reason why the apocalypse is happening is not because they wanted to address it. It's like that because they wanted there to be absolutely no chance to affect things in the larger scale. The same reason the Nation was shattered, it was too global and too impactful.<br /> <br /> This is basically dooming the world, because doing something would matter too much. And boy what a message THAT is XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why I don't like the comparison of Garou in W5 to activists. Because that would make W5 a game about how environmental activism is pointless. The message about the effectiveness of Garou as it's envisioned in W5 is made clear on pg 212 as the book talks about the distinction between systemic (for example, climate change) and local (for example, a pack of BSD) antagonists: &quot;The other axis is that of systemic / individual. Systemic antagonists are large, overarching entities or ideals. Systemic antagonists are massive and often decentralized and, in general, cannot be directly defeated. They can certainly face setbacks at the hands of the characters, but total defeat is almost never an option. Most systemic antagonists have local proxies that can be defeated, thereby hurting the global antagonist\u2019s plans and relieving tension \u2014 the \u201clittle victories\u201d that mean so much in Werewolf, because they address the player characters\u2019 immediate goals.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Werewolf - the Apocalypse: The game about little victories&quot;. Wow, what a tagline...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T13:39:29-07:00","id":1532722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532720#post1532720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Werewolf - the Apocalypse: The game about little victories&quot;. Wow, what a tagline...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>More like &quot;Werewolf the Apocalypse: Even the game would rather be somewhere else.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T14:54:21-07:00","id":1532725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532683#post1532683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, in real life, a lot of crisis actors drive protestors to action that is designed to vilify them. Because, yes, the real change is at the ballot box and contract signings.<br /> <br /> Corporate folk LOVE making the environmentalists into violent loonies.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Crisis actors&quot; is a term that's been co-opted by the right (especially in the U.S.) to tie into a whole lot of vile conspiracy theory nonsense. I'm assuming that you're not meaning it in that sense, but it could definitely be read that way.<br /> <br /> Real-life crisis actors are those hired to play victims for EMS training. I think you're referring to political agitators and counter-protesters here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T15:09:05-07:00","id":1532727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532683#post1532683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, in real life, a lot of crisis actors drive protestors to action that is designed to vilify them. Because, yes, the real change is at the ballot box and contract signings.<br /> <br /> Corporate folk LOVE making the environmentalists into violent loonies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the proper reference here isn't &quot;crisis actors&quot; (as that invokes Alex-Jones-type conspiracy theories) but what I hope you actually meant there is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COINTELPRO\" target=\"_blank\">COINTELPRO</a>. These FBI-operations have different names these days, of course, but the FBI still seems to operate in a similar manner from time to time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T15:44:16-07:00","id":1532730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532725#post1532725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Crisis actors&quot; is a term that's been co-opted by the right (especially in the U.S.) to tie into a whole lot of vile conspiracy theory nonsense. I'm assuming that you're not meaning it in that sense, but it could definitely be read that way.<br /> <br /> Real-life crisis actors are those hired to play victims for EMS training. I think you're referring to political agitators and counter-protesters here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm referring to undercover cops and people paid to start riots and incite violence so the cops can come in and beat protestors.<br /> <br /> Which happens all the time in my area and historically have been a major problem for Civil Rights activists, anti-war protestors, and anti-police brutality people.<br /> <br /> In episonage they're known as Agent Provocateurs but that term gives them way too much romanticisim: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agent_provocateur\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agent_provocateur</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-16-2024, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T15:49:03-07:00","id":1532731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532727#post1532727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the proper reference here isn't &quot;crisis actors&quot; (as that invokes Alex-Jones-type conspiracy theories) but what I hope you actually meant there is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COINTELPRO\" target=\"_blank\">COINTELPRO</a>. These FBI-operations have different names these days, of course, but the FBI still seems to operate in a similar manner from time to time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The FBI's history with them are famous but union busting is where Appalachia has a longer history with them and the regular police never stopped doing so in Kentucky. Nor have the corporations with environmentalists.<br /> <br /> It's pretty common to pay people to go in and be as radical as hell in hopes it makes them make a mistake.<br /> <br /> The mining companies and tobacco companies here have tactics that make Pentex look all too real.<br /> <br /> The reason I bring it up was one of the things that came up when they were trying to arrange BLM protests in my area was that everyone was very much worried about the possibility that people wanted to start some shit in hopes of vilifying the protestors as we certainly saw the media attempt to do so. So it was always encouraged everyone to be on their absolute best behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-16-2024, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T15:56:08-07:00","id":1532732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532731#post1532731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The FBI's history with them are famous but union busting is where Appalachia has a longer history with them and the regular police never stopped doing so in Kentucky. Nor have the corporations with environmentalists.<br /> <br /> It's pretty common to pay people to go in and be as radical as hell in hopes it makes them make a mistake.<br /> <br /> The mining companies and tobacco companies here have tactics that make Pentex look all too real.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in terms of history, we can easily go back to the Pinkertons before that as well to draw some connections. But really, it was just about how calling them &quot;crisis actors&quot; was a poor choice of words on your part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T16:12:28-07:00","id":1532735,"title":"","content":"If we're talking about real life politics, I have to point out that while the powers that be will hire agent provocateurs, forces of the status quo will <i>also</i> malign anyone who takes radical action as agent provocateurs and outside agitators. This happened at BLM and pipeline protests. The government doesn't actually want people blowing shit up; monkeywrenching and ecotage was a grassroots tactic started by committed environmentalists that the state moved heaven and earth to stop. They want people doing their civil disobedience and peaceful protest because that's easier to disregard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T16:29:53-07:00","id":1532736,"title":"","content":"I think that's one of the most disappointing things about W5: It's the Age of Apoycalypse. The world has never been as bad as this... and the game just deflates in the face of that. &quot;Little victories&quot;, &quot;We assume you're gonna just hunker down in a caern at some point.&quot;, &quot;Garou suck at fixing the world.&quot;, &quot;Please don't be too hard on corporations in the so-called capitalocene era.&quot;... yeah, really inspiring stuff from the W5 corebook there.<br /> <br /> The stakes get raised with Age of Apocalypse and this version of WtA has nothing interesting to say in response to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T17:11:08-07:00","id":1532740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532732#post1532732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, in terms of history, we can easily go back to the Pinkertons before that as well to draw some connections. But really, it was just about how calling them &quot;crisis actors&quot; was a poor choice of words on your part.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't surprise me that Alex Jones (I don't listen to him so I don't know his work) co-opts the term. The nature of the Far Right is basically nothing but projection, projection, projection.<br /> <br /> If they accuse someone of being a Satanic pedophile, I fully expect to find a pentagram and imprisoned bunch of children in their basement.<br /> <br /> There's all manner of conspiracies going on among the Far Right but, of course, all the conspiracies blame the left because the people behind their shows are trying to shift blame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-16-2024, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T17:15:18-07:00","id":1532741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532736#post1532736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's one of the most disappointing things about W5: It's the Age of Apoycalypse. The world has never been as bad as this... and the game just deflates in the face of that. &quot;Little victories&quot;, &quot;We assume you're gonna just hunker down in a caern at some point.&quot;, &quot;Garou suck at fixing the world.&quot;, &quot;Please don't be too hard on corporations in the so-called capitalocene era.&quot;... yeah, really inspiring stuff from the W5 corebook there.<br /> <br /> The stakes get raised with Age of Apocalypse and this version of WtA has nothing interesting to say in response to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it says something very clearly that the people who think there is an easy solution with RADICAL ACTION are servants of the Wyrm. That what they plan to do will not only fail but hasten the apocalypse. It may or may not be wrong but the dismissal of groups with valid points as eco-terrorists and criminals is indeed a tactic of the right.<br /> <br /> I remember a bunch of logging activists in my area who got drowned out on the fact the government was destroying some beautiful wilderness with dubious legality because of spiking accusations.<br /> <br /> Personal action may also do nothing while collective action is the only way to make meaningful change. Just like recycling as a person does shit to save the environment and was actually forward by the plastic companies in order to put the onerous of improving the environment on the public versus the corporations that were only ramping up their pollution a hundred times or more.<br /> <br /> Which, of course, comes to two rebuttals:<br /> <br /> 1. That doesn't make a very fun game about being a magic furry Klingon<br /> <br /> 2. Plenty of RL activists do, in fact, consider this to be the absolute wrong attitude to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-16-2024, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T17:30:08-07:00","id":1532742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532730#post1532730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm referring to undercover cops and people paid to start riots and incite violence so the cops can come in and beat protestors.<br /> <br /> Which happens all the time in my area and historically have been a major problem for Civil Rights activists, anti-war protestors, and anti-police brutality people.<br /> <br /> In episonage they're known as Agent Provocateurs but that term gives them way too much romanticisim: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agent_provocateur\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agent_provocateur</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Not disputing that it happens, just disputing your word choice. Crisis actors are a specific thing, and the term is co-opted by right wing extremists to mean another specific thing, neither of which are what we're actually talking about.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T18:41:22-07:00","id":1532743,"title":"","content":"So noted.<br /> <br /> Won't use it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T20:43:12-07:00","id":1532750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532741#post1532741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it says something very clearly that the people who think there is an easy solution with RADICAL ACTION are servants of the Wyrm. That what they plan to do will not only fail but hasten the apocalypse. It may or may not be wrong but the dismissal of groups with valid points as eco-terrorists and criminals is indeed a tactic of the right.<br /> <br /> I remember a bunch of logging activists in my area who got drowned out on the fact the government was destroying some beautiful wilderness with dubious legality because of spiking accusations.<br /> <br /> Personal action may also do nothing while collective action is the only way to make meaningful change. Just like recycling as a person does shit to save the environment and was actually forward by the plastic companies in order to put the onerous of improving the environment on the public versus the corporations that were only ramping up their pollution a hundred times or more.<br /> <br /> Which, of course, comes to two rebuttals:<br /> <br /> 1. That doesn't make a very fun game about being a magic furry Klingon<br /> <br /> 2. Plenty of RL activists do, in fact, consider this to be the absolute wrong attitude to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think it says something that in WtA <i>the ones who do the polluting and destroy the environment are also servants of the Wyrm</i>. And the game shouldn't be about<b></b>: &quot;Please be nicer to the servants of the Wyrm.&quot;. Just because you'd rather pat a Fomor on the head than fight him doesn't mean the Fomor will suddenly do nice things. WtA is heightening the animosity and danger of polluters by associating them with the dangerous spiritual entity of the Wyrm. And so there's a heightening to a similar degree in what Garou are as the opposing force and what they do. Putting the restrictions you'd like to put on IRL-activists on Garou is silly therefore. Garou aren't a one-to-one analogue to IRL-activists, the same way the IRL-polluters aren't mutated freaks with spirit-powers.<br /> <br /> In the case of W5, this brings up two problems where it shoots itself in the foot:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If collective action is supposed to be favored then why is a key-part of W5's setting about Garou failing to do that and mocking that attempt? The Garou Nation is described as a failure and a bad thing (as we can see in the described indiscriminate rejection of the Litany). W5 doesn't think highly of the Garou's attempt at collective action and therefore mocks the idea of collective action being pursued within the game.</li> <li>Rejecting radical action categorically is a pro-status-quo-position. And that just gets you into a position where you end up defending environmental destruction and pollution. Somebody will dump industrial waste into a river while you're arguing it's more important to scold the resistance to that for being too harsh and radical.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T04:10:23-07:00","id":1532841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532683#post1532683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, in real life, a lot of crisis actors drive protestors to action that is designed to vilify them. Because, yes, the real change is at the ballot box and contract signings.<br /> <br /> Corporate folk LOVE making the environmentalists into violent loonies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's where the comparison fails. <br /> In real life, there isn't a bunch of people systematically ravaging labs, quarries and offices, killing hundreds of people at every step. <br /> <br /> Ballot box and contract signing is pretty much useless in the word. Systematically eliminating pentex on the other hand is a functioning tactic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T06:16:29-07:00","id":1532848,"title":"","content":"The thing I've been thinking about with legitimate resistance is and what that looks is the novel Ministry For The Future by Kim Stanley Robinson. It's a very optimistic near-future hard sci-fi take on tackling climate-change. And the one part of that book I was thinking about in particular are the Children of Kali.<br /> <br /> From a blog by Jamie Wheal called <a href=\"https://www.flowgenomeproject.com/post/children-of-kali-and-the-monkey-wrench-gang\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Children of Kali and the Monkey Wrench Gang&quot;</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Both of these books came out within 12 months of each other and were widely regarded as profound commentaries on our current environmental and political crises\u2013\u2013while still offering a measured dose of hope for the road ahead.<br /> <br /> But I couldn't help but notice that both of these books from fingers-on-the-pulse thinkers, included eco-sabotage as core plot points.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> For Ministry for the Future (the title speaks to an imagined branch of the UN situated in Switzerland, dedicated to averting the climate catastrophe) there's all sorts of policy talk and nerdy solutions like a blockchain carbon coin that eventually supplants fiat currencies and helps us abandon petro-economics.<br /> <br /> But...the real needle mover, the intervention that actually changes behavior in this story is a ruthlessly effective eco-terrorist group dubbed the Children of Kali.<br /> <br /> Radicalized by a mass casualty heat event in India (eerily like the one they're having this year), the Children of Kali knock so many Lear jets out of the sky that the Davos crowd grows too scared to use them anymore, and they sink so many container ships that companies switch to giant sailing barges.<br /> <br /> The plot twist by the end is that the Children of Kali and the Ministry for the Future are actually in cahoots, and that the eco-terrorists function as a sort of black-ops arm of the UN Ministry. They can circumvent politics and diplomacy, can call bullshit on cynical stalling tactics, and make those most responsible for the death of the planet feel their own mortality for a change.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Are we past the point of reason?</b><br /> <br /> Just by themselves or taken together, those two books showcasing violent protest should mark a sea change in sentiment. We should note this moment.<br /> <br /> Because the subtext, the story between the lines, is that we're now firmly past the point where reasonable, progressive, civic interventions are going to be remotely adequate to get us out of the fix we're in. Even for the best and brightest thinkers among us.\u200b </div> </div> </div>And I think if you make the setting the Age of Apocalypse, W5 naturally gets to that same line in the sand or question of &quot;Are we past the point of reason?&quot;. This is why Hauglosk and the Cult of Fenris are so ill-suited for this setup. Desperate times call for desperate measures and if you're ramping up the despair with something like an Age of Apocalypse, the list of justifiable acts of resistance becomes equally more radical.<br /> <br /> Also, Ministry for the Future makes clear that violence alone isn't good enough but here's the thing: In WtA, you won't be playing the guys who will solve things on that front. You're playing the scary, violent ecoterrorists who fight against the ones who actively stand in the way of those kinds of solutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T06:29:12-07:00","id":1532851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532848#post1532848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I think if you make the setting the Age of Apocalypse, W5 naturally gets to that same line in the sand or question of &quot;Are we past the point of reason?&quot;. This is why Hauglosk and the Cult of Fenris are so ill-suited for this setup. Desperate times call for desperate measures and if you're ramping up the despair with something like an Age of Apocalypse, the list of justifiable acts of resistance becomes equally more radical.<br /> <br /> Also, Ministry for the Future makes clear that violence alone isn't good enough but here's the thing: In WtA, you won't be playing the guys who will solve things on that front. You're playing the scary, violent ecoterrorists who fight against the ones who actively stand in the way of those kinds of solutions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the book tackles it head on and has a very reasonable position.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Garou have resorted to radical ruthless measure for thousands of years and they have doomed the world. The only solution is to kill all the radicals because even if their heart is in the right place, they are IDIOTS.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is a nice twist on the usual, &quot;Desperate times call for desperate measures.&quot;<br /> <br /> It says the ruthless aren't just wrong, they're dumb because their radical ideas won't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T06:42:39-07:00","id":1532852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532851#post1532851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the book tackles it head on and has a very reasonable position.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Garou have resorted to radical ruthless measure for thousands of years and they have doomed the world. The only solution is to kill all the radicals because even if their heart is in the right place, they are IDIOTS.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is a nice twist on the usual, &quot;Desperate times call for desperate measures.&quot;<br /> <br /> It says the ruthless aren't just wrong, they're dumb because their radical ideas won't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but what you're describing is the definition of half-assed and poorly thought out. That take on &quot;Desperate times call for desperate measures.&quot; would essentially make W5 a game of &quot;The times are desperate - but please don't rise to the occasion.&quot;<ul><li>It's like taking D&amp;D, changing absolutely nothing except within the text of the Players Guide you're making a big deal out of why killing is bad and actually doesn't make things better. And yet D&amp;D will still be a game that's mostly about combat and earning XP for killing monsters. But now the text is whining about how you don't solve anything by killing these monsters. WtA is a game explicitly about raging werewolves confronting things like climate change with direct action. Whining about it just shows a lack of understanding WtA. What's the point of taking a game and making it all about &quot;How about you don't play the game you're currently reading about?&quot;.</li> <li>Okay, so you think radical ruthlessness is bad... now what? What's supposed to be the game about instead now? How are you supposed to solve anything if everything Garou do is automatically bad...? That's just silly...</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","user":"Knightingale","date":". 03-19-2024, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T06:53:02-07:00","id":1532853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532851#post1532851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the book tackles it head on and has a very reasonable position.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Garou have resorted to radical ruthless measure for thousands of years and they have doomed the world. The only solution is to kill all the radicals because even if their heart is in the right place, they are IDIOTS.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is a nice twist on the usual, &quot;Desperate times call for desperate measures.&quot;<br /> <br /> It says the ruthless aren't just wrong, they're dumb because their radical ideas won't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>In legacy, Garou were falling behind because they were hidebound into a set of rules of engagement that prized personal glory on a battlefield of roughly equal forces. Monkeywrenching was the new measure that was presented as actually doing good things and getting results that the Garou needed to happen. The beef with the Fera and need to reconcile was thrown in for good measure.<br /> <br /> It's never been &quot;the Garou are too violent&quot;, but &quot;the Garou have to change what they target with violence&quot;, and they have to do it while venerating their old ways just enough to keep who they are. There's absolutely nothing wrong with sacrificing a bit of glory to make sure that a factory or ship costs more money to maintain than the enemy can reasonably afford.<br /> <br /> Also, consider the source. I know you're probably sick of hearing it, but being directed from the top down by a vengeful Vampire LARP ST certainly does things for the game. and none of them are good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T08:08:14-07:00","id":1532858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532851#post1532851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the book tackles it head on and has a very reasonable position.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Garou have resorted to radical ruthless measure for thousands of years and they have doomed the world. The only solution is to kill all the radicals because even if their heart is in the right place, they are IDIOTS.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is a nice twist on the usual, &quot;Desperate times call for desperate measures.&quot;<br /> <br /> It says the ruthless aren't just wrong, they're dumb because their radical ideas won't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't think this is reasonable at all, at least if your goal isn't &quot;further entrench the status quo.&quot; And to be quite honest, it feels kind of weird to hold this up as a nice twist or a reasonable position. If any ideas are dumb and won't work, it's probably the ideas that we've been trying IRL and haven't been working for the past three decades. If the &quot;radicals&quot; are idiots and should all be killed, exactly what are the moderate Garou doing? Organizing another nonviolent rally? Writing letters to their senator? Running for office? Or just acting as the arms of the cops and the corporations by killing off the radicals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T10:13:23-07:00","id":1532861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532853#post1532853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In legacy, Garou were falling behind because they were hidebound into a set of rules of engagement that prized personal glory on a battlefield of roughly equal forces. Monkeywrenching was the new measure that was presented as actually doing good things and getting results that the Garou needed to happen. The beef with the Fera and need to reconcile was thrown in for good measure.<br /> <br /> It's never been &quot;the Garou are too violent&quot;, but &quot;the Garou have to change what they target with violence&quot;, and they have to do it while venerating their old ways just enough to keep who they are. There's absolutely nothing wrong with sacrificing a bit of glory to make sure that a factory or ship costs more money to maintain than the enemy can reasonably afford.<br /> <br /> Also, consider the source. I know you're probably sick of hearing it, but being directed from the top down by a vengeful Vampire LARP ST certainly does things for the game. and none of them are good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the Garou are ABSOLUTELY too violent.<br /> <br /> * Rage comes from the Beast of War<br /> * The Impergium<br /> * The War of Rage<br /> * DUELS TO THE FUCKING DEATH<br /> * Slaughtering the Bunyip<br /> * The entirety of the war between the European and Native tribes<br /> <br /> The garou were basically Gaia's claws and having killed all of the other tribes, were doing the jobs of the Gural and Bastet and so on crappily.<br /> <br /> W5 taking the position that all of the problems were the Garou supremacy, violent domimace, and isolation from regular humans isn't a bad one.<br /> <br /> It's just...well, none of that is canon anymore so what IS the reason that the Garou were too violent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T11:01:01-07:00","id":1532862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532861#post1532861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the Garou are ABSOLUTELY too violent.<br /> <br /> * Rage comes from the Beast of War<br /> * The Impergium<br /> * The War of Rage<br /> * DUELS TO THE FUCKING DEATH<br /> * Slaughtering the Bunyip<br /> * The entirety of the war between the European and Native tribes<br /> <br /> The garou were basically Gaia's claws and having killed all of the other tribes, were doing the jobs of the Gural and Bastet and so on crappily.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 - Then how does Rage exist in non-Wyrm spirits? The lore books are great but honestly they're dropping the ball hard in trying to sell this notion, especially since some Fera don't even suffer from Thrall of the Wyrm. Note that the description of the Triatic Wyrms is rather odd in expressing material in some respects, such as likening the Biblical Serpent in Eden to the Defiler (a rather egregious mismatch of context going on, there).<br /> 2 - The error wasn't in violence, but in not letting the Ratkin direct it. Killing humans is their thing - frequently through the intermediary of disease or stealing excesses of food (hey look Monkeywrenchers before they were big!), but the existence of their own Warrior Aspect, the Blade Slaves, is a rather stark indicator of &quot;not always, or even uncommonly, or else we wouldn't need these guys.&quot;<br /> 3 - Caused by Garou developing an institutionalized sense of overweening pride and group think. Like 2, the violence was misdirected.<br /> 4 - Which humans still often do! At the very least, it was still common until a century or two ago in major industrialized nations.<br /> 5 and 6 - Nasty result of Garou absorbing the worst parts of modernizing &quot;enlightenment&quot; Europeans (so, basically, Weaver influence) combined with number 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> W5 taking the position that all of the problems were the Garou supremacy, violent domimace, and isolation from regular humans isn't a bad one.<br /> <br /> It's just...well, none of that is canon anymore so what IS the reason that the Garou were too violent? </div> </div> </div>Revised took the position that the flawed Garou were making strides in correcting themselves and hitting the enemy where it actually hurt, but they were racing against the end times. Then Apocalypse happened, and we got a selection of ways to cap off a game of Werewolf in the most final fashion.<br /> <br /> W5 trying to reinvent that without any of the care or connections to prior writing? It's like a worse version of Revised with a lot of pieces and context carved away so as to not overshadow Vampire. It's being forced into a tiny corner because the creative director thinks that it's Wrongbad Fun, and using old indictments of Garou that were being dealt with in Revised to try and sell the result.<br /> <br /> Really, while I'm keen to stand and fight for treasured memories, Apocalypse, the end book, is a hard, if not impossible, act to follow. Some updates to the base system released officially are nice, but no &quot;reimagination&quot; is going to cut the mustard here. The sad joke of PDX's purchase of an end times-flavored horror action IP is that they would have done much better just making their own vampires and what have you, un-troubled by impending ends of the world, because it's obvious that they don't want to address anything calamitous or world-changing. They're just doing some Weekend at Bernie's shit with the games now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T12:24:19-07:00","id":1532863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532861#post1532861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the Garou are ABSOLUTELY too violent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether I agree with this or not, I think it is important to look at the actual game in question. Even W5 is a combat heavy game, shown by the regeneration and the way Rage works.<br /> <br /> The important point is directing that combat to the right sources, not trying to avoid it. Because if you ignore 70% of the game's mechanical focus, you aren't really playing the game, are you?<br /> <br /> In any case, the problem is that W5 isn't really giving any concrete reason TO fight, is it? It is the apocalypse and nothing in the human world has changed. So why bother?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T13:57:11-07:00","id":1532868,"title":"","content":"I mean shattered nation seems to be reversing the corebook stance. Now whether it's just lip service or a full on decent into Garou nationalism we'll find out when the book lunches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T13:11:52-07:00","id":1532952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532861#post1532861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the Garou are ABSOLUTELY too violent.<br /> <br /> * Rage comes from the Beast of War<br /> * The Impergium<br /> * The War of Rage<br /> * DUELS TO THE FUCKING DEATH<br /> * Slaughtering the Bunyip<br /> * The entirety of the war between the European and Native tribes<br /> <br /> The garou were basically Gaia's claws and having killed all of the other tribes, were doing the jobs of the Gural and Bastet and so on crappily.<br /> <br /> W5 taking the position that all of the problems were the Garou supremacy, violent domimace, and isolation from regular humans isn't a bad one.<br /> <br /> It's just...well, none of that is canon anymore so what IS the reason that the Garou were too violent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I gotta disagree with your reading. This isn't because the Garou are too violent. It is because they are too <b>prideful</b><br /> <br /> The Impergium: The belief that the Garou knew what was right for humanity and decided to force the issue with violence and ignored the consequences.<br /> <br /> The War of Rage: The belief that the Garou were the greatest of Gaia's children.<br /> <br /> Bunyip, the Second War of Rage (European and Indigenous Garou wars): European Garou believing that the Indigenous Garou were &quot;too weak&quot; to protect their Caerns and tried taking them. The Brother Tribes were well within their rights to defend themselves and their homes from invaders.<br /> <br /> Duels to the Death: Canonically rare and before that the belief that they'd be numerous for forever<br /> <br /> Rage doesn't come from the Beast of War. Garou Mythology puts it firmly with Luna. Nuwisha myths and Ananasi back this up as both lack Rage entirely. Also mentioned above <b>ALL</b> spirits have access to Rage. Now there are some theories that it is because Gnosis, Willpower, and Rage are originally from the uncorrupted Triat but that still refutes the Beast of War statement. Now Book of the Wyrm 2nd and 20th mention it exists in the Rage of the Changing Breeds we see in 1st it refers specifically in Frenzy. Which seems more likely as all editions of the book mention Vampiric Frenzy as its domain and specifically calls out Frenzying, and this aspect doesn't clash with Rage in spirits, the lack of Rage for a few of the Changing Breeds not associated with Luna or a major celestial body, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28181-a-bunch-of-gamers","name":"A Bunch of Gamers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28181_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T15:57:55-07:00","id":1532967,"title":"","content":"It would generally be more appropriate to say that Rage being directed against allies, used to go on random sprees of senseless violence, and in other ways that actually serve the purposes of the Beast-of-War is what pleases it. That it exists in Rage only when one loses all semblance of control, but not being the root origin of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T20:48:05-07:00","id":1532978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532851#post1532851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the book tackles it head on and has a very reasonable position.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Garou have resorted to radical ruthless measure for thousands of years and they have doomed the world. The only solution is to kill all the radicals because even if their heart is in the right place, they are IDIOTS.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is a nice twist on the usual, &quot;Desperate times call for desperate measures.&quot;<br /> <br /> It says the ruthless aren't just wrong, they're dumb because their radical ideas won't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>So first off, note that the Garou have spent the last several thousand years infiltrating human society, maintaining the veil and generally <i>not</i> engaging in wild, reckless, radical actions. In older editions there were various camps which argued that the fact that werewolves chose to stop engaging in those sorts of actions (like ending the Impergium) is what has allowed the world to progress to its current point where Gaia is now dying.<br /> <br /> Then, going back to the main focus of the thread, the problem that W5 presents the setting as in the middle of the Apocalypse. Gaia is in her death throes (if not possibly already dead), and the gameline presents it as an immediate save Gaia now-or-never crisis. And if the werewolves can't save Gaia <i>right now</i>, then that's it, the world dies and so does everyone and everything they care about. The primary issue is the sense of desperation and immediacy - in otherwords, with the way the Apocalypse is presented.<br /> <br /> In prior editions, where the Apocalypse was on the horizon but not an immediate problem, there wasn't really an issue with characters pursuing longer-term strategies, like Monkeywrenching, to hit companies in their pocketbooks and slowly bleed them dry. But that doesn't feel like it's a reasonable course of action in W5 anymore. Werewolves don't have a timeframe of decades or possibly even centuries to try and save Gaia like they did before. The Apocalypse is happening right this moment, Gaia is going to die in the very, very near future, if again, she isn't already dead and everything is already for naught.<br /> <br /> As such, it seems like the only reasonable course of action is one that's focused on being very direct, and very violent, and long-term, less forceful strategies feel like they'll be a waste of time (by the time those strategies start to pay off Gaia will already be long dead). Remember that with the entire world at immediate risk of dying, werewolves aren't just trying to change the course of one company, or one city, or one country, but need to change the course for every country, and they only have a couple of decades, at best, to do it. It seems like the game presents a setting in which radical and immediate action is the only possible solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-22-2024, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T22:20:04-07:00","id":1532980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Bunch of Gamers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532952#post1532952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, I gotta disagree with your reading. This isn't because the Garou are too violent. It is because they are too <b>prideful</b><br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit off topic here that Sound like a very Elvish flaw?<br /> <br /> Like now that I think about it, the garou do seem pretty Elf coded (or Eldar for any TTS refugees seeing this thread). Like take a look at the following examples<ul><li>Garou are genially portrayed as closer to nature than the other splats.</li> <li>The aforementioned pride that causes the them to screw up horribly in the long run</li> <li>How portion of they race has fallen to a dark power (compare the various take on the dark elf to the Black Spiral Dancers )</li> <li>The dwindling population of the races.</li> <li>How the war of Rage has a similar start to WarHammer Fantasy Battle's War of the Beard (A False Flag by a third party causes existing pollical tensions to degrade into a genocidal war.)</li> <li>How both Garou and elves have pointy ears.</li> </ul>Like if a Dwarf ended up in WOD, he'll reflexivity <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KjHclWPVij0\" target=\"_blank\">insult </a>the garou because they tripped his natural elf sensor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":".  grammer 03-22-2024, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T23:07:46-07:00","id":1532981,"title":"","content":"Garou have been explicitly compared to Tolkien elves in some capacities in the text of the books, yes.<br /> <br /> However, before the dwarf could say anything, the entire lineup of kiths from Changeling would silence them with a single &quot;Ahem,&quot; with the boggans and nockers glaring at them. Some head-shaking may be involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T23:09:21-07:00","id":1532982,"title":"","content":"As stated above, the reason the world is ending is not because garou used violent methods. Rather, it is because garou focused on things other than fighting the Wyrm. To the point where their old methods that USED to work no longer do, because they let the problem be too long in favour of inner-shifter wars.<br /> <br /> It is also always good to remember that garou aren't JUST humans, they aren't JUST focused on making human lives easier. They also have to think of their wolf-kin and other animals, which means that sometimes humans need to go.<br /> <br /> This thread is about the fact that W5 isn't interested in any of that nor is it interested in even addressing the apocalypse. Instead it uses the end of the world to make sure there is no way to actually make a difference if you try to gather up a larger group of garou. It wants a small scale game but in doing so it is saying there is no reason to try beyond your own nose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T00:53:36-07:00","id":1532985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532982#post1532982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is about the fact that W5 isn't interested in any of that nor is it interested in even addressing the apocalypse. Instead it uses the end of the world to make sure there is no way to actually make a difference if you try to gather up a larger group of garou. It wants a small scale game but in doing so it is saying there is no reason to try beyond your own nose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like W5 would work better if it was more explicitly about being a post-Apocalypse setting. In the older editions, the idea was that the characters were fighting to push back the Apocalypse, and every victory meant one more day. But that's not the case in W5, the Apocalypse already happened and the werewolves lost.<br /> <br /> So the focus in W5 is more one about personal survival rather than fighting back. While W5 isn't a traditional &quot;post-apocalyptic&quot; setting, it shares a lot with that genre in terms of themes and mood.<br /> <br /> So the Cult of Fenris is like the remnants of the old government, you might see in a post-apocalyptic game, which is still trying to fight the old war. But that's pointless, since the war already ended and there's nothing but ruins to fit over. Of course the physical world isn't what you would consider apocalyptic yet, but with Gaia dead, the spirit world is dying, and then the physical world will follow after that.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the goal for characters in W5 isn't to save the world, but to survive and to help their loved ones survive, in an increasingly hostile world, one that's inevitably on its way to destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T01:13:01-07:00","id":1532986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532985#post1532985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like W5 would work better if it was more explicitly about being a post-Apocalypse setting. In the older editions, the idea was that the characters were fighting to push back the Apocalypse, and every victory meant one more day. But that's not the case in W5, the Apocalypse already happened and the werewolves lost.<br /> <br /> So the focus in W5 is more one about personal survival rather than fighting back. While W5 isn't a traditional &quot;post-apocalyptic&quot; setting, it shares a lot with that genre in terms of themes and mood.<br /> <br /> So the Cult of Fenris is like the remnants of the old government, you might see in a post-apocalyptic game, which is still trying to fight the old war. But that's pointless, since the war already ended and there's nothing but ruins to fit over. Of course the physical world isn't what you would consider apocalyptic yet, but with Gaia dead, the spirit world is dying, and then the physical world will follow after that.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the goal for characters in W5 isn't to save the world, but to survive and to help their loved ones survive, in an increasingly hostile world, one that's inevitably on its way to destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, that is clearly the intention.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, the game isn't willing to commit to a post-apocalyptic world. Instead, the apocalypse is happening in such a way that the game can still be set in the modern world. It isn't even a slow end of the world like in Wolf's Rain or the end of humanity like in Yokohama KaidashiKik\u014d. The apocalypse only matters to the garou and Hunters and Vampires can ignore it freely.<br /> <br /> So W5 wants there to be no reason for larger scale fights, hence it removed the chance for them. But it also wants to be set in the modern day with the Veil intact. These two things are mutually exclusive, however.<br /> <br /> So W5 has the most meaningless and pitiful apocalypse ever, just so it can have its cake and eat it too.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T01:21:59-07:00","id":1532987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532986#post1532986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So W5 has the most meaningless and pitiful apocalypse ever, just so it can have its cake and eat it too.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And Shattered Nation seems to be starting the process of reversing that stance by giving the PCs tools to Postman back the garou nation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":".  grammer 03-22-2024, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T01:28:52-07:00","id":1532988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532982#post1532982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is about the fact that W5 isn't interested in any of that nor is it interested in even addressing the apocalypse. Instead it uses the end of the world to make sure there is no way to actually make a difference if you try to gather up a larger group of garou. It wants a small scale game but in doing so it is saying there is no reason to try beyond your own nose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most succinct bit where you can see that happening is right there in the Introduction:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eventually this path leads to a view that the world is in a catastrophic state and the time to act may have passed. This generation of Garou dwells in the midst of Apocalypse. It\u2019s too late to avert the end.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s no cause for fatalism, however. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The time to act may have passed.&quot;, &quot;It's too late to avert the end.&quot;... I don't know about you but unlike what the text suggests that sounds pretty darn fatalistic to me. And then it ends with &quot;Otherwise there will be no tomorrow.&quot;. But those two ideas can't both be true at the same time: It either is the Age of Apocalypse where it's too late to avert the end - or it is not.<br /> <br /> But this fence-hopping keeps happening within the book. At one point, it's about the struggle against the odds to make sure there will be a tomorrow like there when it lists what Garou do in W5. That list isn't Apocalypse-themed, it's themed around Garou doing typical Garou stuff as they're fighting back. But then in discussions of the Umbra or the Garou Nation, it's all about &quot;Look how shitty all of this is. This really is the Age of Apocalypse.&quot;. Or when it's saying that it's impossible for Garou to solve systemic problems but they do want Garou-PCs to still deal with local problems as if that matters, as if &quot;small victories&quot; in the face of certain doom matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T02:50:40-07:00","id":1532991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1532988#post1532988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Snip.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean If people want a post apocalyptic WTA game then You should go full gonzo like<a href=\"https://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/general-world-of-darkness-discussion-thread.914481/post-85761416\" target=\"_blank\"> this post</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolf: The Post-Apocalypse<br /> <br /> The Wyrm has won. Gaia is dead. The Weaver is crippled, broken, lobotomized. The Wyld, diminished and corrupted but forever untamed, spews forth an endless river of horrors that even the Wyrm finds grotesque. The Wyrm sits atop the charred husk of the world, lord of all, and yet its victory is pyrrhic. It cannot escape its bonds. It can only stew in its pain and self-loathing. With no other enemies to fight, it turns upon itself. And beneath the Wyrm's notice, life clings and fights for its existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Top of the World.<br /> At the Top of the World sits the Wyrm in all its terrible glory. Its three heads rise up so high that they're visible from all points in the Northern Hemisphere. They constantly bite and tear at each other. None can slay the others, but they all try. As a result, they're covered with wounds that drip foul ichor and where that ichor touches the ground spawn great and terrible Banes. Seasons are no longer determined by the movements of the Earth, but by which of the Heads is dominant.<br /> <br /> The Season of Calamity is also the Season of Growth. It is when farmers plant their corps, and when their crops try to kill them. It is the time when the sky battles the ground, when the wind fights the rain, when trees uproot themselves and turn to slaughter, not that there are many trees left.<br /> <br /> The Season of Consumption is the Season of Harvest, of Glutony, of Famine, of Cannibalism. It is the season when It is the season when parents eat their children not because they are hungry, but merely for the pleasure of the eating. It is the season when the sun shines less, or not at all, it's light eaten before reaching the earth.<br /> <br /> The Season of Corruption is thankfully rare.<br /> <br /> <br /> Motorwolves and Chromebears:<br /> To the very end, Gaia loved her children and it is only natural for children to outlive their parents. Knowing that she was doomed, Gaia made a choice to give her children a chance at the cost of the little life she had left. At the moment the Wyrm manifested on Earth, every living creature on Earth's surface experienced the First Change. Not a drop of changing blood was required, as Gaia was giving her very essence to her children. Extinct breeds walked the earth for the first time since the War of Rage. New breeds never before imagined came into being. Confused and without any sort of leadership or guidance the new Fera were immediately crushed. Most died. Some survived.<br /> <br /> The survivors built new tribes for themselves, made new societies from the ruins of the old. Some crowd around the last fading cairns, hoping that the remnants of Gaia's life force will somehow protect them. Others find safety and power in mobility. They prowl the roads as normads and fight for control of the world's last remaining stores of oil. Elders and Wise Ones talk of a road warrior named Max, a myth from the before time.<br /> <br /> You are a part of a Motorpack. Inspired by the legends of the World Before, you strive to make the Wasteland better than it is, so that others can eek out their livings just a little easier.<br /> <br /> A Non-Exhaustive List of Locations:<br /> The Wyrmlands - Area closest to the Wyrm's domain at the North Pole, where banes constantly war with each other. The Wyrmlands are defined by massive lakes of Wyrmblood fed by the Wyrm's dripping wounds.<br /> The Motorlands - The Wastelands of North America, dominated by nomadic motorpacks. Being so close to the Wyrmlands, the Motorlands suffer from the worst of both worlds, both spiritual monstrosities and personal callousness. The Motorlands' inhabitants find it difficult to accept the possibility of hope, and are in desperate need of legends.<br /> The Ant Empires - South America's rainforsts, still living in spite of the Wyrm's efforts, are dominated by militaristic wereant hives.<br /> The Down Under - Australia, too far away from the Wyrm's emergence point and not important enough to bother with got off relatively unscathed, except for the complete collapse of human civilization. Major cities, unable to feed themselves due to infrastructure collapse, have been abandoned and reclaimed by what is left of nature. </div> </div> </div>TLDR: The world is reduced to a Gamma World style wasteland and most of humanity is converted into fera and have to survive the hell hole earth has become. HAVE FUN!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T07:24:46-07:00","id":1533006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bb