3778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CamaradaDoppio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1533775#post1533775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, is Neoliberal western propaganda. Revolution doesn't work, direct action doesn't work, only the capitalist status quo work, dont try to really change things, only do things that looks like you do things</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I agree and the Russians have a hand in promoting this mindset to sow disunity and apathy in Europe and NA. Like how many &quot;left&quot; media is revealed to have been funded by a Russian oligarch and how many respected professors and speakers will take russians side before they current war with Ukraine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T20:22:52-07:00","id":1533793,"title":"","content":"Again, <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Please refrain from wild accusations and conspiracy theories about design choices. </b></span>\u200bWarnings have been issued.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T05:41:20-07:00","id":1535168,"title":"","content":"On reflection the anti proactive violence message is a little odd in our current situation. Irl were getting to a point were usage if force to prevent a mass extinction event is increasingly plausable. Even if you're not okay with going unibomber petrol bombing the head of bp's house it's hard to object to say sabotaging an oil pipeline in first nation lands.<br /> to quote a friend of mine who becoming increasingly radical &quot;I asked nicely for 10 years, then pleaded for 5.......I'm done asking.&quot;<br /> <br /> W5 avoid this question with a meta reliance on previous editions were violence didn't work, which makes w5 an deconstruction which is frankly irrelevant to irl environmentalism with the new edition and the theme of apocalypse. It might have been more interesting if the young garou were actually the radical group rather then guarding the caern elders","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-06-2024, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-06T11:57:39-07:00","id":1535196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1532650-why-the-apocalypse-in-the-title-matters-and-how-w5-fails-to-address-it?p=1535168#post1535168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On reflection the anti proactive violence message is a little odd in our current situation. Irl were getting to a point were usage if force to prevent a mass extinction event is increasingly plausable. Even if you're not okay with going unibomber petrol bombing the head of bp's house it's hard to object to say sabotaging an oil pipeline in first nation lands.<br /> to quote a friend of mine who becoming increasingly radical &quot;I asked nicely for 10 years, then pleaded for 5.......I'm done asking.&quot;<br /> <br /> W5 avoid this question with a meta reliance on previous editions were violence didn't work, which makes w5 an deconstruction which is frankly irrelevant to irl environmentalism with the new edition and the theme of apocalypse. It might have been more interesting if the young garou were actually the radical group rather then guarding the caern elders</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be an interesting game actually. The old being stale and conservative and the young being brash and reckless. There's a lot of current truamas and opportunities for growth and reconciliation there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"us